        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "SECTION 4.1. For the purpose of this Article 4, a grievance shall be any dispute between the Company and any employee or the Union, involving the interpretation or application of any provision of this Agreement.",
            "block_bbox": [
                184,
                309,
                1062,
                398
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    184.0,
                    309.0
                ],
                [
                    1062.0,
                    309.0
                ],
                [
                    1062.0,
                    398.0
                ],
                [
                    184.0,
                    398.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "SECTION 4.1.1. Such disputes raised by an employee, employees, or the Union may be presented to Management orally or in writing on forms provided by the Union. Names, dates, times, events and other pertinent data necessary for the adequate consideration of the grievance should be stated. Contract provisions allegedly violated should be cited. The nature of the grievance and the remedy sought should be indicated. Technical errors on the grievance form shall not become grounds for denying the grievance.",
            "block_bbox": [
                264,
                420,
                1054,
                648
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    264.0,
                    420.0
                ],
                [
                    1054.0,
                    420.0
                ],
                [
                    1054.0,
                    648.0
                ],
                [
                    264.0,
                    648.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "SECTION 4.2. Oral Grievances: Each grievance which shall come up for the attention of Management shall first be submitted orally to the Supervisor of the employee or employees concerned: (a) Within seven days, excluding Sunday, of the event giving rise to the grievance; or (b) Within seven days after it first became known to the grievant within forty-five (45) days of the event giving rise to the grievance.",
            "block_bbox": [
                179,
                670,
                1064,
                842
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    179.0,
                    670.0
                ],
                [
                    1064.0,
                    670.0
                ],
                [
                    1064.0,
                    842.0
                ],
                [
                    179.0,
                    842.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Section 4.2.1. Regular scheduled work hours spent by the\naggrieved employee and one local Union·Representative pursuant\nto Section 4.2 shall be compensated for at their basic hourly rates of\npay.",
            "block_bbox": [
                262,
                864,
                1065,
                980
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    262.0,
                    864.0
                ],
                [
                    1065.0,
                    864.0
                ],
                [
                    1065.0,
                    980.0
                ],
                [
                    262.0,
                    980.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "SECTION 4.3. Written Grievances – Step 1: In the event said oral grievance shall not be satisfactorily settled within five (5) working days (Monday through Friday) from the date submitted to the supervisor, the same shall then be submitted in writing within seven (7) days, excluding Sunday, to the second level Manager or designee. The grievance shall be in writing on forms provided by the Union, signed by the party or parties or by an authorized Union Representative having such grievance.",
            "block_bbox": [
                177,
                1002,
                1044,
                1201
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    177.0,
                    1002.0
                ],
                [
                    1044.0,
                    1002.0
                ],
                [
                    1044.0,
